  "watch_list": [
    "Oregon data center ballot — Vantage site purchase agreement (Capacity LLC / Will Turner) expires end of September 2026 (~26 days away), five weeks before the November 3 vote; no lawsuit challenging ballot validity reported as of this brief; opposition coalition spans residents, the mayor, and organized labor.",
    "Gordie Howe Bridge — Day 40 of commercial operations as of September 4; Windsor-Detroit Tunnel CEO disclosed August traffic down 12% (4,676 vs. 5,425 average vehicles/day) and projects 7–8% decline in September — first month-level corridor-shift signal; WDBA has still not published its own aggregate crossing data; Ambassador Bridge aggressively locked in carrier contracts during the delay.",
    "One SeaGate — local investors acquired Toledo's tallest building with no redevelopment plans disclosed; any repositioning announcement from new ownership would be among the most consequential downtown announcements of 2026.",
    "Flock cameras — federal class-action lawsuit filed September 2 against Flock Group Inc. alleging 'rampant misuse' of surveillance data; Ohio House bipartisan coalition (Reps. Rader, Brewer, Dean, Pizzulli) letter to ODOT Director Mike Dew asking for statewide freeze on new Flock permits (legislature does not return until after November election); city school pilot in Public Safety Committee following August 27 referral; county contract dispute (commissioners rescinded, sheriff seeking injunctive relief) still unresolved; incoming Chief Braun takes command November 1.",
    "LiveXchange Fall Forum — September 23–25 (19 days away) at Renaissance Toledo Downtown Hotel and Fifth Third Field; first major national site-selection event hosted in Toledo this fall; RGP presenting to corporate location decision-makers.",
    "Brent Industries — 13abc records investigation published September 4 reveals six fires at the South Avenue facility between 2021 and the August 18 blast; Toledo Fire & Rescue found five safety violations in May 2025 inspection with no confirmed follow-up; OSHA investigation ongoing with six-month window (no findings before February 2027); political pressure continuing."
  ],

